   gh release create v0.3.1 --title "v0.3.1: Microbenchmarks" --notes "## v0.3.1: Microbenchmarks - Benchmarking & Observability

   This release introduces comprehensive benchmarking infrastructure for performance analysis and regression testing.

   ### Features

   - **Extended Matmul Sweep**: Problem sizes from 64×64 to 16384×16384
   - **JSON Output**: Structured output for benchmark results (`to_json()` methods)
   - **Extended Tile Sensitivity Analysis**: 13 tile configurations across multiple problem sizes
   - **Standalone CLI Tool** (`kpu-benchmark`): Commands for sweep, tiles, roofline, single benchmarks
   - **Performance Regression Infrastructure**: Baseline management and CI workflow

   ### Benchmark CLI Usage

   ```bash
   # Run extended matmul sweep
   kpu-benchmark sweep --extended

   # Tile sensitivity analysis with JSON output
   kpu-benchmark tiles -f json -o results.json

   # Single benchmark
   kpu-benchmark single -m 2048 -n 2048 -k 2048

   # All benchmarks
   kpu-benchmark all -f csv -o all_results.csv
   ```

   ### Key Performance Findings

   | Problem Size | Best Tile Config | Efficiency | GFLOPS |
   |-------------|------------------|------------|--------|
   | 256×256×256 | 32×64×32 | 78.2% | 800 |
   | 1024×1024×1024 | 32×64×32 | **93.9%** | 962 |
   | 16384×16384×16384 | 64×64×96 | 49.9% | 510 |

   **Key Finding**: Asymmetric tile configurations (32×64×32) significantly outperform symmetric tiles.

   ### Regression Testing

   ```bash
   # Generate baseline
   python scripts/benchmark_regression.py generate

   # Check for regressions (fails if >5% degradation)
   python scripts/benchmark_regression.py check

   # Show comparison report
   python scripts/benchmark_regression.py report
   ```

   ### Files Changed

   - `include/sw/benchmark/benchmark.hpp` - JSON output, extended sweep functions
   - `tests/benchmarks/test_matmul_benchmarks.cpp` - Extended tests
   - `tools/benchmark/kpu-benchmark/benchmark.cpp` - CLI tool
   - `scripts/benchmark_regression.py` - Regression testing
   - `.github/workflows/benchmark-regression.yml` - CI workflow

   ---
   **Full Changelog**: https://github.com/stillwater-sc/kpu-sim/compare/v0.2.0...v0.3.1"
